Enhance an existing React chat/run screen in this codebase. The screen
currently lets a user select task modules, pick a repository, type a prompt,
and execute an AI agent run. Today it shows a flat activity log, an empty
"waiting for output" result panel, and duplicate "RUNNING" status badges
scattered across several cards. Do not add new backend calls — reuse the
existing state, props, and websocket/polling data the screen already
receives. Refactor the presentation only, keeping all current functionality
(module selection, repo field, prompt input, execute action, log display,
result display) intact.

Restructure the screen as follows:

1. Consolidate status: remove all duplicate "RUNNING" badges. Add ONE
   telemetry strip below the page header with stat cells: run status
   (pulsing live dot + run ID), elapsed time (ticking), total tokens
   in/out if available, steps complete (e.g. 3/5), and retry count.
   Monospace font, tabular numerals. If a metric isn't available in
   existing state, render the cell with a "—" placeholder.

2. Move the existing configuration controls (module checkboxes, repository
   field, prompt textarea, execute button) into a collapsible left rail
   (~270px, collapses to a thin strip). While a run is active, show the
   execute button as disabled with "run in progress".

3. Replace the flat activity log with an execution trace: a waterfall/
   Gantt view on a shared time axis. One row per pipeline step: status
   dot (done / running / pending), step name, a time-span bar positioned
   by start time and duration, duration + token count right-aligned.
   Derive rows from the existing log/step events; if start/end timestamps
   exist, position bars proportionally, otherwise fall back to equal-width
   segments. The running step's bar grows over time with a subtle animated
   gradient; done bars are muted; pending steps show dashed ghost bars.
   Show an amber "retry N" badge on any step with more than one attempt.
   Rows are clickable to select.

4. Below the trace, add a split pane: left = live log tail for the
   selected step (timestamped lines, amber highlight for timeout/retry
   lines, blinking cursor on the last line while running); right = the
   result panel upgraded with tabs (Report / Artifacts / Raw JSON).
   While the run is incomplete, show any partial output already produced
   plus a note that the final result is pending — never a bare empty state.

5. Add a slim status footer: connection status, environment name, and
   keyboard hints in small monospace text.

Visual direction: dark mission-control aesthetic. Very dark desaturated
green-black background (#0B100E), warm off-white text (#E4EBE6), 1px
hairline borders (#1F2B25). One luminous jade (#3BE39B) reserved ONLY for
live/running activity; completed = muted jade, pending = dim outline.
Amber (#F0B45B) for warnings/retries, soft red for the abort action.
Grotesque sans (e.g. Archivo) for UI labels, JetBrains Mono for all data,
IDs, timestamps, and logs. Uppercase 10px letter-spaced eyebrow labels
for section headers. Animations limited to: pulsing live dot, gradient
sweep on the active bar, blinking log cursor — respect
prefers-reduced-motion. Keep all controls keyboard-focusable with visible
focus rings.

Preserve existing routing, API calls, and state management. Ship this as
a presentational refactor of the current screen's components.
